<title>UK: Licht sees Polish sugar consumption rising in 96/9.</title>
<headline>Licht sees Polish sugar consumption rising in 96/9.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sugar consumption is likely to rise in Poland in 1996/97 due to the higher production level, German statistician F.O. Licht said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Because of the high level of production, consumption is also likely to rise in Poland, while some unregistered cross border trade may also help to swell apparent domestic needs,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>In its second estimate of the world sugar balance for 1996/97, Licht said production in Poland -- eastern Europe's third largest beet sugar producer -- had reached around 2.5 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Poland's sugar production in 1995/96 amounted to 1.69 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
